###############################################################################
#
# ADCIRC coupled + FULL one-way NWM river forcing via the dnwm CDEPS component
# (USE_NUOPC_RIVER, connected path): DATM + ADCIRC(OCN) + NWM(dnwm) + MED.
#
# Same case as coastal_ike_shinnecock_atm2adc, plus the NWM/dnwm data component
# and the direct NWM -> OCN redist connector, so the ADCIRC cap receives a
# per-NODE volumetric discharge field (river_volume_flux, m3 s-1) and converts
# it to the per-unit-width normal flux QNIN on IBTYPE 22/32 boundary strings
# instead of reading fort.20.
#
# ID CONTRACT (redist / mapfcopy: no area weighting, sequence index == receiver
# global id): the dnwm mesh has ONE ENTITY PER ADCIRC GLOBAL NODE in natural
# node order 1..NP, and the stream carries a full-size sparse array that is zero
# everywhere except the river-boundary nodes.
#
# REQUIRES (Phase 0 artifacts staged into the run; generated by
# logs/adcirc_nwm/gen_adcirc_nwm_phase0.py):
#   - INPUT/adcirc_node_ESMFmesh.nc  (one element per ADCIRC global node; order
#     == ADCIRC global node id == the redist contract)
#   - INPUT/nwm_discharge.nc         (river_discharge(time,nnode) [m3/s])
#   - a fort.14 with at least one IBTYPE 22/32 normal-flux boundary string, and
#     a fort.15 whose NFFR/flux bookkeeping matches it
# Build with -DUSE_NUOPC_RIVER=ON. See ADCIRC_NWM_RIVER_FORCING.md.
#
# NOTE: full RT auto-staging (default_vars.sh export_dnwm_cdeps + run_test.sh
# atparse of dnwm_in.IN / dnwm.streams.coastal.IN + fv3_conf staging of the
# Phase-0 files) is NOT yet wired -- exactly the same status as the SCHISM test
# coastal_ike_shinnecock_atm2sch_nwm_cdeps. Stage dnwm_in, dnwm.streams and the
# two Phase-0 NetCDF files by hand for a first connected run. Both the COMPILE
# and RUN lines in rt_coastal.conf stay commented until that gap is closed and
# a baseline exists.
#
# meshloc: this test MUST use meshloc=node (the sibling coastal_ike_shinnecock
# _atm2adc uses element). The ADCIRC cap applies the single OCN `meshloc`
# attribute to every field (ADCIRC_RealizeFields -> ESMF_FieldCreate(...,
# meshloc=meshloc)) and therefore refuses to realize a CONNECTED
# river_volume_flux unless meshloc=node -- the redist contract below is per NODE,
# and ADCIRC_ImportRiver additionally asserts
# size(river_volume_flux ptr) == mdataIn%NumOwnedNd. With meshloc=element the run
# aborts in ADCIRC_RealizeFields with ESMF_RC_NOT_VALID. `node` is also the cap's
# own default when the attribute is absent, and it matches the met-field import,
# which already indexes owned NODES (owned_to_present_nodes / NumOwnedNd).
# Consequence: the ATM -> OCN half of this test is NOT bit-comparable to
# coastal_ike_shinnecock_atm2adc; that is the one deliberate divergence.
#
###############################################################################

